WIRE.md §2.2 rule 1, TYPES.md §13.4: an unrooted asset root starts at the directory of the file
declaring the asset type, so items/icons/a.png is found; the project root's icons/ is not
consulted (b.png is there only), and E3701 prints the root's display path (WIRE.md §2.3).
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- items/item.canon --
/// Items.
package items

/// Item.
record Item {
  /// Icon.
  icon: asset("icons", ext: [png])
}

/// Items.
let items: stable table Item = {
  sword { icon: "a.png" }
  shield { icon: "b.png" }
}
-- items/icons/a.png --
-- icons/b.png --
-- build.txt --
error[E3701]  items/item.canon:13:18
  items.shield.icon: asset b.png not found under items/icons
  expected by items/item.canon:7 (icon: asset("icons", ext: [png]))

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
